---
/*
 * Footer status badge → the public status page (https://status.myne.md).
 *
 * Neutral label by design: it never asserts an uptime state ("System status",
 * not "All systems operational"), so it can't be wrong during an incident — the
 * live state lives on the status page itself. It inherits the footer's
 * mono/uppercase/size/colour; only the dot and the hover colour are its own.
 * The site is static and status.myne.md sends no cross-origin header, so this is
 * a link, not a live fetch (see the footer-status decision).
 */
---

<a
  class="status-badge"
  href="https://status.myne.md"
  target="_blank"
  rel="noopener noreferrer"
>
  <span class="status-badge__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  System status
</a>

<style>
  .status-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 7px;
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
    /* The badge is the middle child of a space-between footer bar
       (© · badge · version). margin-left:auto absorbs the free space on its
       left, so the badge and the version that follows it sit side by side on
       the right, with the copyright alone on the left — instead of all three
       being flung to the edges. */
    margin-left: auto;
  }
  .status-badge:hover {
    color: #e6e6e4;
  }
  .status-badge__dot {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #5fbf8f;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(95, 191, 143, 0.16);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
</style>
